{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534095-v20-thaumaturgy-rituals-questions","id":1534095,"title":"[V20] Thaumaturgy Rituals Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-12T08:36:11-07:00","id":1534095,"title":"[V20] Thaumaturgy Rituals Questions","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have questions about rituals:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can an object have multiple <b>Ward versus X</b> active?<br /> Having both Ward versus Ghouls AND versus Kindred active on it.</li> <li>Is there any restriction on the size, shape, material or use of the <b>Ward vs X</b>?<br /> I am envisioning a grapple build in which your clothes and gloves are warded, so you just need to touch the relevant creatures to start hurting them... Would a punch cause even more damage? Or place it on portable things like ball bearings and just throw them at enemies (Movement of the Mind seems useful here).</li> <li><b>Warding Circle versus X</b>, can it be centered on a portable object? Or it is stuck to the ground relative to when it was casted?</li> <li><b>Shaft of Belated Quiescence</b> and <b>Enchant Talisman</b>, can both be combined? If so, what happens with your talisman if the tip is broken, does it lose the enchantment?</li> <li>The Gargoyle write up on <i>Lore of the Bloodlines</i> says that an <b>Enchant Talisman </b>ritual can be casted on a Gargoyle, the ritual description says you can only have a single talisman:<ul><li>Does enchanting a Gargoyle, stops you from having your own regular Talisman?</li> <li>Can a Gargoyle have multiple <i>permanent </i>Ward vs X rituals on itself, or does it need to activate one by one as per the writeup?</li> <li>Is the Gargoyle treated as the caster Talisman and grants the benefits to the caster with touch; or is the Gargoyle considered to be its own talisman, and get the talisman benefits on itself?</li> </ul></li> </ol>Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-14-2024, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T17:58:46-07:00","id":1534218,"title":"","content":"Any takers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T02:26:37-07:00","id":1534234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534095-v20-thaumaturgy-rituals-questions#post1534095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can an object have multiple <b>Ward versus X</b> active?<br /> Having both Ward versus Ghouls AND versus Kindred active on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there is no rule that demands exclusivity. Each ward has to be placed separately and has its own warding glyph.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534095-v20-thaumaturgy-rituals-questions#post1534095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any restriction on the size, shape, material or use of the <b>Ward vs X</b>?<br /> I am envisioning a grapple build in which your clothes and gloves are warded, so you just need to touch the relevant creatures to start hurting them... Would a punch cause even more damage? Or place it on portable things like ball bearings and just throw them at enemies (Movement of the Mind seems useful here).</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules are vague in that they don't specify what counts as 'an object', but that is nothing unusual for these rituals (usually ST's call). As written there are no restrictions on material or shape. Melee weapons and projectiles can be warded, but the rules imply that the warding glyph may be broken by continued use. In DA:V a three success roll on Melee is required after combat for the glyph to stay intact, so for gloves and clothes I would probably go with Brawl.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534095-v20-thaumaturgy-rituals-questions#post1534095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Warding Circle versus X</b>, can it be centered on a portable object? Or it is stuck to the ground relative to when it was casted?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's stationary. The idea is to either ward large areas (your Haven) or create a magic circle to trap entities like the classic summoning circle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534095-v20-thaumaturgy-rituals-questions#post1534095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shaft of Belated Quiescence</b> and <b>Enchant Talisman</b>, can both be combined? If so, what happens with your talisman if the tip is broken, does it lose the enchantment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything I know about WOD sorcery and magic says that breaking it would destroy the enchantment, even if breaking is a function of the object like with Shaft. Not a good combo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534095-v20-thaumaturgy-rituals-questions#post1534095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gargoyle write up on <i>Lore of the Bloodlines</i> says that an <b>Enchant Talisman </b>ritual can be casted on a Gargoyle, the ritual description says you can only have a single talisman</div> </div> </div> </div>The choice of Enchant Talisman as the Ritual for enchanting Gargoyles was imo a bad choice by the writers. The Ritual is meant to create a spell focus for the sorcerer, which is a unique item that differs from other enchanted objects due to the intimate connection it has with the caster. The DA:V version of the Ritual literally mentions the caster will put a piece of their soul into it, and Gargoyle Rituals use a completely different process in DA:V. It was probably done to streamline the system, but as mentioned, it's not a good fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534095-v20-thaumaturgy-rituals-questions#post1534095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Gargoyle treated as the caster Talisman and grants the benefits to the caster with touch; or is the Gargoyle considered to be its own talisman, and get the talisman benefits on itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>The intention is to provide the Gargoyle with the ability to store spell patterns they can use when needed. Magic plug-ins if you will. I would probably take that aspect of the Enchant Talisman Ritual and treat it as otherwise separate from its use to create personal spell focus, including the additional benefits it provides.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534095-v20-thaumaturgy-rituals-questions#post1534095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does enchanting a Gargoyle, stops you from having your own regular Talisman?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go with the above interpretation, no. Otherwise it's the ST's call.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534095-v20-thaumaturgy-rituals-questions#post1534095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Gargoyle have multiple <i>permanent </i>Ward vs X rituals on itself, or does it need to activate one by one as per the writeup?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can have multiple wards, but they need to be activated individually.<br /> <br /> For enchanting Gargoyles I recommend checking out the DA:V Storyteller's Companion which is a lot more detailed on the subject and offers an alternative system. It also has a bunch of exclusive Rituals for Gargoyles.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T17:48:33-07:00","id":1534277,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> thanks for your reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}